  <prov:wasInformedBy rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/wine_prov#TestGenerationActivity"/>
  <prov:wasAssociatedWith rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/wine_prov#agent_OntoGeneration_Agent"/>
  <prov:hadRole rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/wine_prov#GeneratorRole"/>
  <prov:hadPlan rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/wine_prov#GenerationPrompt"/>
  <prov:qualifiedAssociation>
    <prov:Association>
      <prov:agent rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/wine_prov#agent_OntoGeneration_Agent"/>
      <prov:hadRole rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/wine_prov#GeneratorRole"/>
    </prov:Association>
  </prov:qualifiedAssociation>
  <vaem:rationale>The ontology models all supplied classes, properties, and individuals to answer each competency question in one step. Classes form a taxonomy under Wine and Characteristic. Object properties link wines to their attributes, vintages, and grapes, with inverse relations and disjointness as specified. Individuals Bordeaux and NapaZinfandel are typed as Wine. Every property carries explicit domain and range axioms, and all proposed class axioms are materialized on their subjects.</vaem:rationale>
</prov:Activity>

